{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/407680-how-does-switching-covers-affect-bodily-needs","id":407680,"title":"How does switching covers affect bodily needs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-16T06:35:57-08:00","id":407680,"title":"How does switching covers affect bodily needs?","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Demon's can have multiple covers, but they can't have multiple covers active at the same time. When a cover isn't active, it's my understanding that it basically doesn't exist. These bodies have the normal needs to eat and sleep, etc. Demon states that Demons aren't used to these needs. But what happens when you switch covers? Does the active cover have the same needs as the previous one?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Example: if I have covers A and B, and A is hungry and I switch to B, is B hungry? Or does A remain hungry the next time I switch to A (like a low battery I swapped out but still needs to charge)? Or perhaps neither is true, and when you switch back to A it is no longer hungry.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">My biggest thought isn't really food but sleep: can a demon get away with not sleeping by switching to another cover?</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 02-16-2015, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T08:09:01-08:00","id":407767,"title":"","content":"I'm going to say no, since I'm pretty sure injuries aren't healed by Cover-switching. Bodily things presumably remain constant through the switch. So I'm tired and hungry and switch to Cover B. I eat and sleep before returning to Cover A, which is no longer tired or hungry. It holds up time-wise. While A was inactive and unseen, it's logical to assume A slept. <br /> <br /> For some biological things that might be really confused by gender-switching, I guess it's best to just assume they don't resume when you switch back but continue while the Cover is in sleep-mode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T08:51:44-08:00","id":407812,"title":"","content":"I personally won't put a hard answer on it. It depends a lot on a lot of things. Like, if one Cover had a stomach flu, I wouldn't make all of them sick. In the end, I go with &quot;whatever is currently story appropriate&quot; and &quot;doesn't contradict previous rulings.&quot; Consistancy and whatever makes the story flow is my answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T09:01:07-08:00","id":407817,"title":"","content":"I think tracking covers' sleep and eating separately would become a headache after a while. I mean, imagine switching from one late at night, and then switching back in the middle of the day and being dead tired. Much easier to have it follow between forms. <br /> <br /> Now, in the case of time spent in demon form, <i>that </i>I might count as sleep/eating, on the basis that taking the form heals and recharges the demon. And also so spending the night like that doesn't result in jetlag the next day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T10:45:02-08:00","id":407943,"title":"","content":"Hunger and fatigue are constant across Covers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T12:00:10-08:00","id":408008,"title":"","content":"I'd disagree with that ruling, because I can't really see what having migrating hunger and sleep would do to help with a game. I can also tell you that my demon has a 'regular job' with high cover that's very fun, but rarely gets involved in weird stuff like lizardmen living in the sewers. For that, I wait until she sleeps and switch to my street person cover, doing odd questy stuff while my 'real life' is sleeping.<br /> <br /> That helps me a ton and also has produced a lot of very interesting game situations, so if anybody out there is running, I suggest you make hunger / sleep cover specific because it allows you to have seven hours or so in a heavy-cover identity where you can actually do things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T12:28:51-08:00","id":408062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/407680-how-does-switching-covers-affect-bodily-needs?p=408008#post408008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd disagree with that ruling, because I can't really see what having migrating hunger and sleep would do to help with a game. I can also tell you that my demon has a 'regular job' with high cover that's very fun, but rarely gets involved in weird stuff like lizardmen living in the sewers. For that, I wait until she sleeps and switch to my street person cover, doing odd questy stuff while my 'real life' is sleeping.<br /> <br /> That helps me a ton and also has produced a lot of very interesting game situations, so if anybody out there is running, I suggest you make hunger / sleep cover specific because it allows you to have seven hours or so in a heavy-cover identity where you can actually do things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression the difficulty of maintaining multiple Covers was part of the downside and danger of having many. A feature, not a bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T12:54:06-08:00","id":408096,"title":"","content":"Some problems are interesting and produce good narrative to share between covers... like glitching. Others are sorta boring and not very interesting narrative to share... like pooping. I get more out of the game by having a seven hour period to be a homeless crazy drifter occasionally than I think we would by enforcing a strict bedrest policy, but obviously your mileage may vary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T13:13:02-08:00","id":408113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/407680-how-does-switching-covers-affect-bodily-needs?p=408096#post408096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some problems are interesting and produce good narrative to share between covers... like glitching. Others are sorta boring and not very interesting narrative to share... like pooping. I get more out of the game by having a seven hour period to be a homeless crazy drifter occasionally than I think we would by enforcing a strict bedrest policy, but obviously your mileage may vary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough!<br /> <br /> It does raise the interesting idea of having an Embed or Exploit that could split your &quot;natural functions&quot; between Covers. In which case the whole idea would become opt-in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T14:24:54-08:00","id":408192,"title":"","content":"When I say that needs are consistent across Covers, I'm not advocating applying those needs harshly. Outside of <i>Vampire</i>, I don't usually emphasize the need to eat in the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T22:44:00-08:00","id":408625,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer, it'll be what I'll run the game with, if I ever get to run it. I have additional thoughts that need to escape my brain though, so sharing them below.<br /> <br /> Thinking the battery concept could be interesting and cause interesting problems (if paperwork headaches). I'm thinking of the story where the demon doesn't like sleep. Now imagine if they could avoid it with a different cover, each cover can stay up for ~24 hours IIRC, before fatigue rolls. They don't want to sleep, they keep using covers and trying to get and trade more covers like a junkie. Or maybe you have 3 covers, you stay up for 70 hours different covers working on a problem, now you've got an angel coming, and you're going to have to sleep for 36 hours...<br /> <br /> Of course even not requiring sleep by cover switching can cause problems when you're night job runs later than your day job starts... hey honey, where'd you go last night, I rolled over and you were gone...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T04:29:21-08:00","id":409882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/407680-how-does-switching-covers-affect-bodily-needs?p=407943#post407943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunger and fatigue are constant across Covers.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about things like poison, or disease? Specifically, mortal diseases such as cancer?<br /> <br /> Edit: Found it in the book, diseases and poison sray with the demon across cover. Therefore, to get rid of a mortal disease, the demon would have to use an exploit. <br /> <br /> However, there is a story in Interface, where a demon takes a disease from a human via a pact, before presumably blowing this cover and loosing the disease. Therefore I assume that if a disease is patched in with a pact, it belongs to the cover instead of the demon.<br /> <br /> Another interesting question would be if a demon suffers from fatigue etc. in deminic form. I'd say no, because the demon's body is no longer human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1125,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","user":"gflash","date":". 02-18-2015, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T05:02:33-08:00","id":409929,"title":"","content":"Poison is a tilt, right? I think tilts stay on the cover that got them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T08:45:35-08:00","id":410131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/407680-how-does-switching-covers-affect-bodily-needs?p=409929#post409929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poison is a tilt, right? I think tilts stay on the cover that got them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not necessarily. Some conditions / tilts stay with the Cover, some affect the demon specifically. <br /> <br /> Like, a Crippled Condition shouldn't apply to all Covers, since it wouldn't make sense for John Doe to suddenly have one leg like Jane Harris, a newly adopted soul pact. <br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb, I go with What Would Michael Weston Do? Think of Covers more as just a really fancy mask you wear - you are still just one person. If you're being Poisoned, you, the fallen-angel-spy &quot;Michael Weston&quot; is going to be poisoned, and any personas you adopt are going to be going to still be poisoned. If he's acting like the accountant Frank Dias, who's got asthma and needs an inhaler, then the Cover is going to be under an appropriate Condition. <br /> <br /> Its all just a glorified act, though. Enhanced via quantum magic so the act has physical consequences, maybe, but still a glorified act. <br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the &quot;real person&quot; will be getting hungry, tired, cranky, sick, hurt and so on under all these Cover &quot;masks.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}